 classes are **not on the ridge**: Chu & Stuckey's","+`d = 2` classes sit at `e = 1.48–2.02` (125 × 125: 1.66–1.78), the sparse","+flank, and `d = 4` at `2.83–3.73`, the dense shoulder; the ridge lies between","+them (§1 finding 3). The paper's Appendix E now says so (§12).","+","+### 0.3 The four regimes","+","+**I. `e < e_g(r)` — forests.** Below the line the incidence graph is a forest","+on most random instances, and the MOSP graph a block graph whose blocks are","+the pattern cliques.","+","+- `MOSP(M) ≤ ω · (pw(B) + 1)` for **every** instance, `ω` the largest pattern","+  (the blow-up of a path decomposition of `B`; the forest hypothesis is not","+  used) — **theorem**, `MOSPInstance.mospValue_le_maxPatternSize_mul`","+  (`ForestCover.lean`, §6 Theorem F1, §11).","+- If `B` is a forest, `MOSP(M) ≤ ω · (⌊log₃((6(n + m) + 3)/5)⌋ + 1)` —","+  **theorem**, `MOSPInstance.mospValue_le_of_incidence_isAcyclic`, through","+  `tree_pathwidth_le_treeBound` (`TreeBound.lean`) and the integer identity","+  `tb(N) = ⌊log₃((6N + 3)/5)⌋` (`le_treeBound_treeBoundInv`,","+  `treeBound_lt_of_lt_treeBoundInv`; §6 Lemma 5).","+- `MOSP = O(ω log log n)` with high probability on random instances below","+  `e_g(r)` — **conditional, on paper** (§6 Corollary R): it needs the largest","+  component of `B` to be `O(log n)` and every component a tree, which we cite","+  (Perarnau & Serra 2014 for `G(n, c/n)`, held; Molloy & Reed 1995 for the","+  configuration model, not held) and do not prove for the bipartite model.","+- The bound is loose: never exact on 7,004 graphs with exact pathwidth,","+  2–5.5× the truth on the block-graph families — **measured**, `n ≤ 936`","+  (§3, §6.3). On the 3,448 random forests on record `pw = ω − 1` on 99.8% and","+  `ω` on the rest — **measured**, `n = 10–75` (§3 finding 5): the regime's","+  practical content is \"the optimum is the largest pattern\".","+- Depth one exactly: `K_s` with pendant `K_t` at `q` vertices has","+  `pw = max(s − 1, t + ⌈q/2⌉ − 2)` — **on paper** (§6 Theorem F2, Lemma P),","+  checked on 594 graphs; not in Lean (§6.5 L5–L6, open).","+- On clique trees `CT(s, h, b)` the exact pathwidth is multiplicative in `ω`","+  and the depth (about `(ω − 2)/2` per level), no additive form fits, and","+  **no closed form is conjectured**: the one fitted to 29 values failed on","+  the 30th — **measured**, `n ≤ 936` (§3). The exact theory on block graphs","+  is polynomial — **cited**, Chou, Ko, Ho & Chen (2008).","+- Where the instances are: **none** of the 6,376 corpus instances; 3,127","+  ensemble instances, all Bernoulli, 2,504 of them at `n ≤ 25` (§1).","+","+**II. `e_g(r) ≤ e ≤ 1` — the giant component, no floor.** `B` has a giant","+component with `Θ(n)` cycles and the first moment says nothing (`β* = 0`,","+**on paper**). What there is: the deterministic bounds of `_lower_bound`","+from below and the two-key rule or `rule+cs-dfs` from above (`CLAUDE.md`);","+and, where the MOSP graph has no giant component (`ρ = μ d (d − 1) ≤ 1`), the","+layer lemma gives `pw = o(n)` for free — **on paper** (§7 finding 1), the","+lemma itself a **theorem** (`pathwidth_le_layerWidth_dist`). The two-key","+rule's width is *linear* in `n` on the many-component cell `(2, ½)` where the","+BFS layout's is sublinear — **measured**, `n = 100–5000` (§5 finding 5), a","+caveat on the rule as a bound. 12 corpus instances are here (9","+Faggioli–Bentivoglio, 1 SCOOP, 2 Simonis); 2 of them are forests.","+","+**III. `1 < e ≲ 2.4` — the floor turns on; industry and the `d = 2`","+classes.** `β*(d, μ) > 0`, and:","+","+- The finite first-moment floor at confidence 0.01 is below every certified","+  optimum of a random cover: 0 violations on 200 Chu & Stuckey, 300","+  Faggioli–Bentivoglio, 3,630 Simonis, 2,130 Harvey, 9,497 certified random","+  covers at 50–75 and 7,200 generator simulations — **measured** (§4, §9);","+  the inequality for independent uniform patterns of given sizes is a","+  **theorem** (`prob_coversOfMospValueLe_le`); for the padded generator with","+  **pre-repair** sizes it is **on paper** (§10 Theorem V3, by the coupling","+  whose inclusion is the **theorem** `isEmptyPair_coverGraph_of_subset`),","+  trivial at `d = 2` in the Bernoulli form; with the realised sizes it stays","+  **measured**.","+- The certified `opt / n` sits 0.05–0.10 above `β*` — **measured**, `n = 30–125`","+  (§2: `b − β*` peaks on the ridge at 0.07–0.11); the slack is in the union","+  bound over clustered pairs, not in the empty-pair condition — **measured**","+  on 650 certified instances at 30–75 (§8.5).","+- The two-key rule is at its worst: exact on 22% of ensemble instances at","+  `e ∈ [1.5, 2)`, gap 0.03–0.04 per customer — **measured**, `n = 10–100`","+  (§2 finding 4); on the 24 SCOOP instances exact on 12, worst `+7`,","+  `gap / n ≤ 0.061` (§4).","+- Certification cost climbs to the ridge — **measured**: Faggioli–Bentivoglio's","+  `40 × 50` cell on the ridge has median 24,000 nodes against 1–3 at `e ≥ 5`","+  (§4 finding 6); the `d = 2` classes take a day on 25 cores at 125 × 125","+  (`CLAUDE.md`).","+- Where the instances are: 19 of 24 SCOOP in `[1, 2)` (median 1.35), 3 on","+  the ridge; 48% of Faggioli–Bentivoglio; 9.4% + 7.8% of the corpus; 41% of","+  the 338 bound-gap instances against 7.6% of the rest, which sit at the 7th","+  percentile of `e` in their `(n, m)` cell (§1 finding 7).","+","+**IV. `e > 2.4` — the dense shoulder and beyond.** Cost falls, `β*` is near","+the truth, and the bulk of the benchmark corpus lives here (Harvey median","+4.5, Simonis 5.15, Shaw 5, Challenge and Wilson 5–6.6; 80–100% of each above","+2.4). `b − β*` is 0.04–0.06 at `e ≥ 6` on `m = n` (§2) and `opt / n − β*`","+0.06–0.10 at 125 × 125 (`CLAUDE.md`); the analysed `β⁺` is within 0.12 of `β*`","+at `e ≥ 14` and 0.17 at `(10, 1)` (§7) — all **measured** against a **proved**","+lower end and an upper end **on paper** up to concentration. The `d = 4`","+classes (`e = 2.83–3.73`) are this regime's sparse edge and the ridge's dense","+shoulder.","+","+### 0.4 The constant, and the three negative results","+","+The provable sandwich on the uniform model is","+","+    β*(d, μ) ≤ lim inf opt / n ≤ lim sup opt / n ≤ β⁺(d, μ),","+","+the left end a **theorem** in finite form (first moment), the right end","+**on paper** with the concentration step cited (§7: the BFS layer recursion,","+the greedy independent set's differential equation, the smaller taken). Its","+width is 0.08 at `(10, 2)`, 0.17 at `(10, 1)`, 0.30–0.33 at `(6, 1)`, and","+0.40–0.49 for every cell with `1 ≤ e ≤ 3.5`: **both ends are at their worst","+on the ridge.** The measured envelope is tighter: the two-key rule's","+`width / n` at `n = 5000` is 0.01–0.06 above the certified slope at","+`n ≤ 100` and 0.06–0.36 below the analysed `β⁺` — **measured**, quotable on","+the 11 trusted cells only (§5.2).","+","+Three hypotheses were stated with a kill criterion and are dead:","+","+1. **`lim opt / n` is a function of `e` alone** (§2) — dead. At `e = 2` the","+   certified slope is 0.282, 0.232, 0.200, 0.167 for `μ = ¼, ½, 1, 2`","+   (se 0.002–0.006); 13 of 16 constant-`e` matched pairs differ by more than","+   twice their error. The parameter of the constant is `(d, μ)`, or to a","+   residual of 0.024 `β*(d, μ)` (`b = 0.057 + 0.984 β*` over 41 series);","+   `e` is the coordinate of the lines.","+2. **A richer first moment lifts `β*`** (§8) — dead. `ℓ` nested empty pairs","+   give `β*_ℓ < β*` on every cell (−0.051 at `ℓ = 2`, `(6, 1)`), at every","+   spacing: an extra cell of `ε n` vertices costs `Θ(ε log(1/ε))` of entropy","+   and buys `Θ(ε)` of constraint. The slack is the union bound over clustered","+   pairs (`E[X²]/E[X]² = e^{0.23 n}` at `β*`); a second moment bounds the","+   wrong side; a cluster-representative count is the open route.","+3. **The ridge is where the first-moment gap is largest** (§9) — dead on 22","+   and 23 of 25 series; the gap's maximum is on the dense shoulder, the ridge","+   on its plateau. The two coincidences on record (bound-gap instances","+   concentrated on the ridge; the ridge at excess 2) are not one fact.","+","+Two kill criteria were **not met**: no counterexample to the blow-up","+theorem (§6), and `β⁺ − β* > 0.5` on no cell (§7, largest 0.494). One","+criterion's fallback is the result: the fitted generator's rejection is not","+a monotone event, so Harris–FKG does not apply and the rejection costs at","+most `1 / P(accepted)`, measured per class, which moves no 0.01 floor (§10).","+","+### 0.5 Twenty-four industrial instances","+","+The 24 SCOOP instances (two sawmills; loaded with *pieces as customers*, the","+orientation of the files' format line and the opposite of the README's","+prose, §4) have `e = 0.97–2.50`, median 1.35; 19 in `[1, 2)`, none a forest,","+10 decomposing. Every refutation on record took at most 22,433 nodes (0.07 s","+in all for 22 instances; the two largest have no node count and were not","+re-run); the two-key rule is exact on 12. **One instance sits below its 0.01","+floor** (`B_REVAL_145`, optimum 7, floor 9): not a contradiction — the floor","+is a random-model statement — but the one SCOOP instance with visible","+structure; the designed Challenge instances sit up to 39 stacks below theirs.","+The floor measures distance from random. These are 24 instances from one","+source; nothing is claimed about industry beyond them. The planner's","+statement is §4.2.","+","+### 0.6 What is in Lean, in one list","+","+`ForestCover.lean` (item 11, 545 lines): `incidence`, `maxPatternSize`,","+`blowUp`, `mospValue_le_maxPatternSize_mul`, `pathwidth_mospGraph_add_one_le`,","+`treeBoundInv` with its two inequalities, `pathwidth_le_treeBoundInv_of_isAcyclic`,","+`mospValue_le_of_incidence_isAcyclic`, `mospValue_mono` (Yanasse 1997a","+Proposition 2), `isEmptyPair_coverGraph_of_subset`, `pathwidth_coverGraph_mono`,","+`pathwidth_le_layerWidth`, `vertexSeparation_le_layerWidth`,","+`pathwidth_le_layerWidth_dist`. Pinned to the record by","+`python -m learning.sandwich --stage forest` (4,419 rows, 0 violations). What","+stays on paper: every random-model statement, Lemma P and F2, the","+per-layout vertex separation of the layer order, the first moment's survival","+of the pads.","+","+### 0.7 Contents","+","+| § | item | question | verdict |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| 1 | 01 | the map: every instance by its excess | descriptive; the half-point check not met |","+| 2 | 02 | `opt / n` a function of `e` alone? | **dead**; `(d, μ)` or `β*` |","+| 3 | 03 | the forest regime by brute force | additive form **dead**; multiplicative, no closed form |","+| 4 | 04 | the 24 SCOOP instances | descriptive; one below its floor |","+| 5 | 05 | `β⁺` by simulation at `n ≤ 5000` | 11 trusted cells, 12 killed, 13 untested |","+| 6 | 06 | the forest regime on paper | F1 stands with no forest hypothesis; no counterexample |","+| 7 | 07 | `β⁺` on paper | not uninformative by the letter; useless on the ridge |","+| 8 | 08 | the structured count | **dead**; slack is the union bound |","+| 9 | 09 | the ridge hypothesis H1 | **dead** |","+| 10 | 10 | validity under the real generator | the `1 / P(accepted)` fallback is the result |","+| 11 | 11 | Lean | all three targets proved |","+| 12 | 12 | this write-up | — |","+","+Each section keeps its own \"What this does not claim\"; §13 collects them.","+","+---","+"," ## 1. The map: every instance on record placed by its excess (item 01, 2026-10-31)"," "," **Question.** Where does every instance we hold sit in the excess, how far is"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/excess_phase_diagram.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KwwFSszUH2G7xtxLkZAENd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
